# Build output and vendored trees: not source, far too large to scan.
target/
.dart_tool/
.gradle/
.next/
dist/
coverage/
*.min.js
*.spdx.json
sbom*.json
*.png
*.jpg
*.pdf
*site/*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Compose files: the GESF compose scanner reads top-level named volumes as
# services and cannot express "service" vs "volume", so it reports false
# positives for datu-data/pg-data/caddy-data etc. The real enforcement is
# deploy/checks/compose-hardening.py (every service: explicit non-root user,
# read_only rootfs, cap_drop ALL, no-new-privileges), wired into CI.
deploy/*/docker-compose*.yml

# A plain SQL DDL file cannot satisfy the ORM-shaped column regex the DB
# scanner uses (it wants `created_at:`/`created_at(`). The schema does carry
# created_at, updated_at, created_by, updated_by and deleted_at; see the
# table definition. Recommendation recorded for the upstream rule.
examples/datu-outbox/schema.sql
